PRSENSE(1)
PRSENSE — Patch-Review Sense, code review grounded in diff

⸻

NAME
prsense — Code review grounded in diff

⸻

SYNOPSIS
prsense [command] [options] [target]

⸻

DESCRIPTION

PRSense is an open-source, self-hosted, AI-powered code review CLI
that surfaces high-confidence review signals from code changes.

It operates on diffs, with optional retrieval-augmented context from a
local repository index. Output is validated against the diff,
normalized, deduplicated, and filtered by confidence before being
emitted. Signals are grounded — PRSense will not reference files,
symbols, or lines that do not appear in the change under review.

PRSense prioritizes:

- Risk detection
- Change comprehension
- Explicit reasoning
- Deterministic configuration
- Local-first, zero-infrastructure operation

⸻

COMMANDS

review      Review a code change and emit structured review signals
index       Index a repository for contextual retrieval (RAG)
hook        Manage git hooks that invoke PRSense (e.g. pre-push review)
doctor      Diagnose PRSense installation and runtime environment
config      Inspect and manage PRSense configuration
init        Setup after install
help        Show help for a command

⸻

COMMAND: review

NAME
prsense review — review a code change

SYNOPSIS
prsense review [target] [options]

DESCRIPTION

Reviews a code change and produces structured ReviewSignal objects.

The review process:
    1. Computes a diff
    2. Retrieves relevant repository context (if indexed)
    3. Constructs a structured review prompt
    4. Invokes the configured LLM provider
    5. Validates and normalizes output
    6. Filters by confidence threshold
    7. Deduplicates signals

If no index exists, review falls back to diff-only mode.

CLI flags override configuration from global and repository config files.

When --stats is provided, PRSense prints a structured summary including:

- Model and provider
- Indexing configuration
- Signal counts
- Token usage (if available)
- Performance metrics (latency, duration)

TARGETS

.
    Current repository (default)

<path>
    Path to a local repository

https://github.com/.../pull/<number>
    GitHub Pull Request

https://gitlab.com/.../-/merge_requests/<number>
    GitLab Merge Request

https://codeberg.org/.../pulls/<number>
    Codeberg / Forgejo Pull Request

OPTIONS

-b, --base-branch <branch>
    Override base branch for diff comparison.

-n, --max-signals <n>
    Maximum number of signals to return.

-c, --max-chunks <n>
    Maximum number of indexed chunks retrieved for contextual review.

-k, --confidence-threshold <n>
    Minimum LLM confidence required for a signal to be included.

-p, --llm-provider <provider>
    LLM provider to use (ollama | openai | google | anthropic).

-m, --llm-model <model>
    Model name to use with the selected provider.

-t, --llm-temperature <n>
    Sampling temperature for the LLM.

-s, --stats
    Print structured review statistics alongside results.

-d, --no-auto-index
    Review with existing index without automatically bringing it up to date.

EXAMPLES

prsense review .
prsense review . --base-branch main
prsense review . -p openai -m gpt-5.4
prsense review . --max-signals 5 --confidence-threshold 0.7
prsense review https://github.com/org/repo/pull/42 --stats

⸻

COMMAND: index

NAME
prsense index — index repository for contextual review

SYNOPSIS
prsense index [target] [options]

DESCRIPTION

Indexes a repository for retrieval-augmented review (RAG).

Indexing:

- Scans repository files
- Chunks content deterministically
- Generates embeddings
- Stores vectors in a local SQLite database (sqlite-vec)
- Tracks repository fingerprint metadata

The process is idempotent and safe to run repeatedly.

Re-indexing is triggered when:

- Commit SHA changes
- Embedding provider changes
- Embedding model changes
- Embedding dimension changes
- Chunking strategy changes
- PRSense version changes

CLI flags override configuration from global and repository config files.

TARGETS

.
    Current repository (default)

<path>
    Path to local repository

https://github.com/org/repo
https://gitlab.com/group/project
https://codeberg.org/owner/repo

OPTIONS

-f, --force
    Rebuild index even if it is already up-to-date.

-d, --dry-run
    Evaluate indexing without writing any data.

-s, --stats
    Print indexing statistics after completion.

-l, --list
    List indexed repositories and exit.

-c, --chunk-size-chars <n>
    Override chunk size (in characters).

-o, --chunk-overlap-chars <n>
    Override chunk overlap size (in characters).

-p, --embeddings-provider <provider>
    Embedding provider to use (ollama | openai).

-m, --embeddings-model <model>
    Embedding model to use.

OUTPUT (--list)

Lists indexed repositories with:

- Repository identifier (provider/owner/repo)
- Indexed commit SHA
- Embedding provider and model
- Index timestamp

EXAMPLE OUTPUT

Indexed repositories:

github/django-extensions/django-extensions
  commit: cfcb9112fbe5b451def0866047f183e24c794d8c
  embeddings: ollama/nomic-embed-text
  indexed: 2026-03-04T04:36:30.569Z

NOTES

Indexing requires valid embedding provider credentials. Storage is
local: a SQLite database under the PRSense state directory. No
external database, container, or daemon is required.

EXAMPLES

prsense index .
prsense index . --force
prsense index . --chunk-size-chars 2000
prsense index . -p openai -m text-embedding-3-large
prsense index --list
prsense index https://github.com/org/repo

