COMMAND: hook

NAME
prsense hook — manage git hooks that invoke PRSense

SYNOPSIS
prsense hook install   [--force]
prsense hook uninstall
prsense hook status

DESCRIPTION

Installs and manages a git pre-push hook that runs PRSense against
each pushed ref before the push completes. The hook gates pushes on
review outcome, with bypass available via `git push --no-verify`.

The installed hook is a small, version-marked shim. It reads git's
standard pre-push input from stdin and invokes `prsense review` once
per pushed ref, scoped to the diff between the local and remote
commits. Branch deletions are skipped. New branches fall back to the
configured base branch.

Hook resolution honors `core.hooksPath`, worktrees, and submodules.
When `core.hooksPath` is set (e.g. by Husky or lefthook), PRSense
emits a warning before installing into the managed directory.

SUBCOMMANDS

install
    Install the pre-push hook for the current repository.

    Refuses to overwrite a non-PRSense hook unless --force is given.
    Upgrades a previously-installed PRSense hook in place when the
    shim version has changed.

uninstall
    Remove the PRSense pre-push hook. Refuses to remove a hook not
    installed by PRSense; remove such hooks manually.

status
    Report installation state: not installed, installed and current,
    installed but out of date, or present-but-foreign. Prints the
    resolved hook path.

OPTIONS

-f, --force
    (install only) Overwrite an existing non-PRSense pre-push hook.

ENVIRONMENT

PRSENSE_NON_INTERACTIVE
    Set to 1 to suppress first-run setup prompts. The installed hook
    sets this automatically so `git push` never hangs on an uninitialized
    PRSense configuration.

REQUIREMENTS

- Git 2.31 or newer (checked at runtime).

EXAMPLES

prsense hook install
prsense hook install --force
prsense hook status
prsense hook uninstall

NOTES

The hook is opt-in. Once installed, every `git push` from the
repository triggers a PRSense review of the pushed diff. The push
proceeds if no blocking signals are emitted and is rejected
otherwise. To bypass for a single push:

    git push --no-verify

