COMMAND: doctor

NAME
prsense doctor — diagnose environment and configuration

SYNOPSIS
prsense doctor

DESCRIPTION

Performs structured diagnostic checks:

- Configuration validation
- Credential validation
- Local index storage
- LLM provider configuration
- Repository state

Each check emits structured, actionable results.

EXAMPLES

prsense doctor

⸻

COMMAND: config

NAME
prsense config — inspect and manage PRSense configuration

SYNOPSIS
prsense config inspect

DESCRIPTION

Inspects PRSense configuration as resolved at the current working
directory. Useful for debugging unexpected behavior, verifying which
layer contributed a given value, and confirming credential availability
without exposing secrets.

SUBCOMMANDS

inspect
    Print the effective configuration with provenance annotations.

    Output includes:

    - Each configuration field with its resolved value and source layer
      (default, global, repo, env, or cli)
    - Credential availability per provider (never the secrets themselves)
    - Any validation warnings

    Configuration sources are layered, lowest to highest priority:

        defaults  <  global  <  repo  <  env  <  cli

    Internal-only paths (e.g. resolved repository root) are omitted from
    the output.

EXAMPLES

prsense config inspect

⸻

CONFIGURATION

PRSense separates:
    1. Review behavior configuration (repository-level)
    2. Runtime credentials (environment)

USER CONFIGURATION

A file named prsense.yml may be placed at repository root.

Example:

llm:
  provider: ollama
  model: deepseek-coder-v2
  temperature: 0.1

embeddings:
  provider: ollama
  model: nomic-embed-text

review:
  confidenceThreshold: 0.8
  topSignals: 3

index:
  auto: true
  chunkSizeChars: 1000
  chunkOverlapChars: 200

context:
  maxChunks: 5

git:
  baseBranch: main

If absent, sensible defaults are applied.

ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES

Environment variables configure credentials.

Common variables:

PRSENSE_OPENAI_API_KEY
PRSENSE_GOOGLE_API_KEY
PRSENSE_ANTHROPIC_API_KEY
PRSENSE_OLLAMA_HOST
PRSENSE_GITHUB_TOKEN
PRSENSE_GITLAB_TOKEN
PRSENSE_CODEBERG_TOKEN
PRSENSE_GITHUB_BENCH_TOKEN
PRSENSE_LOG_LEVEL
PRSENSE_NON_INTERACTIVE

Environment variables are validated before workflows execute.

⸻

EXIT STATUS

0   Successful execution
1   Invalid configuration or usage
2   Runtime failure

⸻

FILES

prsense.yml
    Repository-local configuration.

~/.config/prsense/
    Optional user-level configuration.

~/.local/state/prsense/
    Runtime state directory (includes the local index database).

<git-hooks-dir>/pre-push
    PRSense pre-push hook shim, when installed via `prsense hook install`.
    Location resolved via git (honors core.hooksPath and worktrees).

⸻

DESIGN PRINCIPLES

PRSense is intentionally:

- Local-first
- Self-hosted
- Retrieval-augmented
- Deterministic
- Structured in output
- Explicit in configuration
- Focused on high-signal review

It prioritizes signal quality over verbosity.

